.TH HTTP_HEADER 3
.SH NAME
http_header \- add a header to the request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int http_header(http* " h ", const char* " name ", const char* " value ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_header ()
adds the line "name: value" to the request that was started last. It must be called before
the request is sent.
.P
The module itself writes the request line, Host (with the port if it is not the default one),
Connection (close, unless
.I keepalive
is set), the framing of the body (Content-Length or Transfer-Encoding: chunked) and
"Accept: */*", the last one only when no Accept header was added. Everything else is up to the caller:
Content-Type, Authorization, User-Agent, ...
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 if there is no request, the memory is short, or if name is empty or has a colon, or name or value has a CR or LF in it (they would split the header or end it).
.SH SEE ALSO
http_open(3), http_body(3), http_chunked(3)
